    "created_at": "2021-02-11T16:29:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-11T16:29:18Z",
    "body": "We have a few popular websites that are basically unusable with HW-backed canvases (we have cases like CAD applications that do UI in Canvas2D or MIT Scratch). In those cases, these sites are really dependent on `getImageData` for performance.  It's weird to have sites that unless fall into some non-specified heuristic can't be accessed (we are not talking 60 to 30 fps drop here, this is more like: 60fps to 1fps).\r\n\r\nWe'll gather some hard numbers to show this.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
