    "body": "Hi all, I just read the update at https://developer.chrome.com/blog/canvas2d/#will-read-frequently\r\n\r\nI think a guideline is necessary for the average developer so it doesn't get abused - specifically at what point should a developer consider setting it to true? Spec/sites like MDN should provide the recommended 'threshold' for consideration.\r\n\r\nAs an example I have a script that copies frames from a video element at a ~33ms interval to canvas and I'm processing pixel data via getImageData - is this an applicable use case?\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
